# BSI — the first module-composition PFS proof flavor (pubid#706 §4): the
# British Standards face composed from the module library. BSI is THE
# flagship composition story — British Standards adopting EN/ISO/IEC
# documents (`BS EN ISO 13485`, `BS EN IEC 61851-1`, the national.prefix
# head over the en.overlay adoption over the adopted inner document) —
# and the bsi corpus is the biggest composition corpus in the fleet
# (1,500 cases; tests/bsi in pubid-testsuite).
#
# The composition (issue #706 §4, grammar#122's port shape):
#
#   national.prefix  — the "BS" head token as DATA (the module's
#                      parameter), the same module DIN/NF/SS- compose with;
#   en.overlay       — the EN adoption face and its identity (the adopted
#                      document is the base), routing to the inner modules;
#   iso.inner        — the adopted ISO document face ("BS ISO 8601:2019");
#   iec.inner        — the adopted IEC document face ("BS IEC 60747-8");
#   supplements.core — the amendment/corrigendum operators as bindings
#                      (BSI's "+A1:2016" spelling, plus-separated).
#
# edition.core is NOT bound: its edition_face requires an
# `edition_space` separator the composing definition must supply, and
# BSI's ED face is GLUED to the number ("BS HD IEC 60364-8-81 ED1" — no
# separator exists to supply). The face is declared where the wrapper
# owns it instead — under `adopted.edition` — the hook lifting the
# trailing ED ordinal out of the adopted run onto the wrapper column.
#
# The coded Pubid::Bsi flavor carries machinery beyond grammar
# composition (the 1,495-line builder): the typed-trio serialization
# (PAS/PD/DD/TS rows carry type/stage/typed_stage with harmonized
# stages), the wrapper attribute named `base` (the uniform parent
# accessor), the RootIdentity MR slugs, the root-through URN reads,
# the nested publisher body form, and thirty-plus families outside the
# composition surface (aerospace, Flex, index/method/section suffixes,
# national annexes, Expert commentary, bundles, sets). Those are the
# MEASURED boundary — the parity harness (spec/pubid/bsi_pfs/) classifies
# every non-parity row against this definition's corpus.
#
# What the composition DOES absorb, and compiles here: the national
# head over the adoption chains (BS EN…, BS EN ISO…, BS EN IEC…, BS
# HD…, DD CEN ISO/TS…, DD CLC/TS… — the adopted run delegated to the
# owning flavors through the §4 coded hook), the plain BS face with
# parts and years, the PAS/PD/DD/TS designations, the face-only
# standalone-AMD designation ("AMD 11015" — issue #151's tier-B family,
# `designation: face`: the head token selects the class and prints the
# face while nothing serializes beyond _type, the coded
# StandaloneAmendment's own {_type, number}), BSI's plus-separated
# amendment run, and the wrapper-with-adopted identity of the adoption
# face.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The tier-B/C ledger (issue #151): every corpus family the composition
# does NOT absorb, with the fail-closed reason it cannot compose under
# the declared surface today. The rows stay pinned in pubid's
# spec/pubid/bsi_pfs/parity_spec.rb (653 unabsorbed after the AMD
# composition); a family composes only by ADDING the declaration
# surface it needs, never by relaxing a parity expectation.
#
#   COMPOSED under v2:
#   standalone_amendment (4) — the face-only designation (above).
#
#   FAIL-CLOSED — second-scheme surfaces (a family that is its own
#   scheme, composed as its own definition when it lands, not as
#   declarations on this one):
#   aerospace_standard (339) — the aerospace series (2S/3S/4S/A/B/C/G/
#     T/TD heads, the AVD variants, CISPR routing); a whole sub-
#     vocabulary of heads and number shapes.
#   flex (23) — "BSI Flex 1886 v2.0:2024-09": its own head, the dotted
#     v-version and the year-month date.
#
#   FAIL-CLOSED — needs a declared surface v2 does not carry:
#   bundled_identifier (27) — the member run: members are WHOLE
#     documents with per-separator capture ("; ", " and ", " & ",
#     " TO "/" to "), synthesis modes ("BS 1580:Parts 1 and 2" builds
#     the base + part members; "BS 2SP 68 to BS 2SP 71" repeats the
#     head; "BS 9113 N001 to 004" is a zero-padded range). The
#     supplements run carries kind+ordinal items, never documents.
#   national_annex (18) — "NA to BS EN 1996-1-2:2005": a SECOND
#     wrapper-with-adopted face (the `adopted:` dispatch is single per
#     definition) whose base is itself an adoption chain, plus the
#     NA's own amendment run between head and base ("NA+A1:2014 to
#     BS EN 1997-1:2004+A1:2013").
#   committee_document (6) — "14/30300822 DC": the designation token is
#     TRAILING (after the number), the 2-digit year expands by a
#     century rule (a semantic decode — the facets ruling keeps decode
#     rules out of the declared surface), and the family's official-URN
#     profile differs (no type-abbr/stage segment; the purn token is
#     cd). Needs trailing-token designations and per-type URN profiles.
#   addendum_document (22) — "BS 2000-0:Addendum No.  1:1983": the
#     No.-worded addendum face with double spaces, three separators
#     ("-", " ", ":"), the mid-face base year ("BS 449-2:1969 Addendum
#     No.  1:1975") and the typed addendum_year column.
#   supplement_document (18), explanatory_supplement (1) — the worded
#     run ("Supplement No. 1") and the inverted headless form
#     ("Supplement No. 1 (1970) to BS 1831:1969").
#   expert_commentary (25), index (13), supplementary_index (1),
#     method (14), test_method (6), section (11) — trailing suffix
#     faces after the year ("Expert commentary", "Index [Issue n]",
#     "Method nnnn", "Sections a and b") and the worded sub-numbering
#     runs; trailing suffix faces are not a declared surface.
#   detailed_specification (16) — the N-series sub-designation
#     ("BS 9210 N0009-1:1978": zero-padded N ordinal with a dashed
#     sub-number) as a face of its own.
#   disc (9) — the escalation prefix before the designation ("DISC PD
#     0005:1995"); a prefix chain the head dispatch does not carry.
#   set (1) — the coded Set's own serialization raises
#     (IncorrectModelError, the cross-flavor member type pinned in
#     pubid's wrapper-root-number hand-off); composing the parse would
#     flip the RAISE signature the parity harness pins, so it stays
#     outside until the coded model is repaired.
#   value_added_publication (6) — the parenthetical value-added
#     suffixes ("(Book)", "(R2004)").
#
#   FAIL-CLOSED — the four declared shapes (same reasons, row-level):
#   the AMD keyword supplement face ("BS 7671 AMD2", the plus members
#     "BS EN 60335-2-27 AMD2", the letter ordinal "AMD AA") — a
#     space-separated keyword face inside the plus run, which the run's
#     face-digit item grammar refuses;
#   the second_number slash column ("BS 4300/10:1967", "PD 6430/1:1970")
#     — a slash sub-number the face does not declare;
#   the CISPR aerospace routing ("BS CISPR 12:1997") — the coded flavor
#     routes CISPR to the aerospace series, so the composed flavor
#     refuses it rather than mis-representing the class;
#   the parenthetical suffixes ("PD 6079-4:2006 (Book)").
#
#   FAMILY RESIDUALS — the rows inside otherwise-absorbed families fail
#   under the same reasons: british_standard's 42 (the "BS 2316-1 and
#   2"-shaped bundles, the addenda/supplements, the BS 4300/n slash
#   series, the "BS 2011-3A & B" part alternation), consolidated_'s 46
#   (the AMD-keyword members above), adopted_international_'s 7 (the PD
#   CISPR TR adoptions), published_document's 2 (the slash column and
#   the parenthetical suffix). The draft "Draft BS" face remains a
#   declared negative and a follow-up item.

pfs: 1

scheme: bsi
title: "BSI (module composition)"

organization:
  name: "British Standards Institution"
  publisher: "BS"
  # The head-dispatch tokens the composed flavor ACCEPTS: the national
  # body token (national.prefix as data) and the BSI designation faces
  # that are their own head tokens (PAS/PD/DD/TS — the publisher-type
  # faces, cen's CR/CWA rule). The escalation prefix DISC and the Flex
  # series stay outside this surface.
  prefixes: ["BS", "PAS", "PD", "DD", "TS"]

# The §4 composition: the inner ISO/IEC faces, the EN adoption overlay
# over them, the national body token as data, and the supplement/edition
# operators as bindings.
modules:
  - module: iso.inner
    version: 1
  - module: iec.inner
    version: 1
  - module: en.overlay
    version: 1
  - module: national.prefix
    version: 1
    parameters:
      prefixes: ["BS", "BSI"]
  - module: supplements.core
    version: 1

# The deliverable faces (feature 1). The token-free BritishStandard is
# the default class; the designation faces are publisher types (feature
# 5); the adoption wrappers (feature 4) have no tokens of their own —
# the hook builds them for every adopted run.
types:
  british_standard:
    key: bs
    web: british_standard
    title: "British Standard"
    short: "BS"
    tag: "pubid:bsi:british-standard"
    publisher_default: "BS"
    stage:
      code: pubbs
      stage_code: published
      abbr: ["BS"]
  adopted_european_norm:
    key: aen
    web: adopted_european_norm
    title: "Adopted European Norm"
    short: "EN"
    tag: "pubid:bsi:adopted-european-norm"
    publisher_default: "BS"
    adopted: true
  adopted_international_standard:
    key: ais
    web: adopted_international_standard
    title: "Adopted International Standard"
    short: "BS"
    tag: "pubid:bsi:adopted-international-standard"
    publisher_default: "BS"
    adopted: true
  # The typed trio (the designation shape): the token selects the class
  # but is not a publisher — the column keeps the organization default
  # ("BS", the coded trio's runtime publisher) and the identifier carries
  # the declared stage's type/stage/typed_stage (the coded
  # TYPED_STAGES rows, harmonized stages included). The printed face
  # prints the designation itself.
  publicly_available_specification:
    key: pas
    web: publicly_available_specification
    title: "Publicly Available Specification"
    short: "PAS"
    tag: "pubid:bsi:publicly-available-specification"
    tokens: ["PAS"]
    designation: true
    stage:
      code: pubpas
      stage_code: published
      abbr: ["PAS"]
      harmonized_stages: ["60.00", "60.60"]
  published_document:
    key: pd
    web: published_document
    title: "Published Document"
    short: "PD"
    tag: "pubid:bsi:published-document"
    tokens: ["PD"]
    designation: true
    stage:
      code: pubpd
      stage_code: published
      abbr: ["PD"]
      harmonized_stages: ["60.00", "60.60"]
  draft_document:
    key: dd
    web: draft_document
    title: "Draft Document"
    short: "DD"
    tag: "pubid:bsi:draft-document"
    tokens: ["DD"]
    designation: true
    stage:
      code: pubdd
      stage_code: published
      abbr: ["DD"]
      harmonized_stages: ["60.00", "60.60"]
  technical_specification:
    key: ts
    web: technical_specification
    title: "Technical Specification"
    short: "TS"
    tag: "pubid:bsi:technical-specification"
    tokens: ["TS"]
    designation: true
    stage:
      code: pubts
      stage_code: published
      abbr: ["TS"]
      harmonized_stages: ["60.00", "60.60"]
  # The face-only designation (issue #151, the tier-B standalone-AMD
  # family): the head token selects the class and prints the face, and
  # NOTHING serializes beyond _type — the coded StandaloneAmendment is
  # exactly {_type, number} (no publisher, no type/stage/typed_stage;
  # its TYPED_STAGES row is internal). `AMD` is a HEAD token here, a
  # different position from the supplement-operator spellings the
  # reserved list guards (publisher/prefixes/keys/stage abbreviations —
  # none claimed; the amendment run keeps its own A/C faces).
  standalone_amendment:
    key: sa
    web: standalone_amendment
    title: "Standalone Amendment"
    short: "AMD"
    tag: "pubid:bsi:standalone-amendment"
    tokens: ["AMD"]
    designation: face

# The wire shape (the coded BSI flavor's own): the publisher column
# serializes NESTED ({"body": "DD"} — the adoption rows' publisher), so
# the flat-scalar table the cen shape applies is declined here.
serialization:
  flat_publisher: false

# The adopted-base dispatch (feature 4): the hook is vendored beside the
# generated classes (lib/pubid/bsi_pfs/adopted_base.rb) — it parses the
# adopted run with the OWNING flavor (EN/CEN/CLC/HD/ENV/ES/CR/CWA leads
# through Pubid::CenCenelec, ISO through Pubid::Iso, IEC/CISPR through
# Pubid::Iec), picks the wrapper class by what came back (a CEN
# identifier is an adopted European norm; an ISO/IEC identifier an
# adopted international standard), and carries the multi-level chains
# (BS EN ISO … is a BSI wrapper over a CEN adoption over the ISO
# document — the identity composition the modules declare). The adopted
# document lands on the uniform `base` column (the coded wrapper's
# slot — the codec's root-first walk, the from_hash key and the MR join
# all read it); the wrapper's identity is ROOT-THROUGH (the official-URN
# identity segments and the MR hooks read the origin document:
# urn:bsi:bs:1073:-2:2002, bs.1073-2.2002); and the wrapper's own glued
# edition face ("BS HD IEC 60364-8-81 ED1") is lifted from the adopted
# run by the hook.
adopted:
  field: adopted
  attribute: base
  hook: coded
  identity: root_through
  edition:
    face: "ED"
    separator: " "

# BSI's supplement spelling (feature 3): the plus-separated amendment
# run ("BS 10125:2014+A1:2016", "BS EN 1005-1:2001+A1:2008") folds into
# the consolidated bundle; the corrigendum face C exists in the coded
# flavor (no corpus rows) and is declared beside the amendment. The AMD
# keyword spelling (" BS 6305:1992 AMD1" — a space-separated face) and
# the "/AMD1" IEC-internal runs stay outside: a slash cannot START a
# declared item (the face-digit item fails on "AMD1"), so those runs
# stay inside the adopted capture where the owning flavors parse them.
supplements:
  run: supplements
  item: supplement
  kind: supplement_kind
  number: supplement_number
  number_kind: string
  date: [year]
  wrappers:
    amendment:
      face: "A"
      tag: "pubid:bsi:amendment"
      title: "Amendment"
      fields: [year]
      mr: [amd, number, year]
      urn: [amd, number, year]
    corrigendum:
      face: "C"
      tag: "pubid:bsi:corrigendum"
      title: "Corrigendum"
      fields: [year]
      mr: [cor, number, year]
      urn: [cor, number, year]
  consolidated:
    tag: "pubid:bsi:consolidated-identifier"
    title: "Consolidated identifier"
    # The coded-BSI bundle shape: no marker word — the members' segments
    # append directly (urn:bsi:bs:10125:2014:amd:1:2016), the MR slug is
    # the base document's own, and the members carry the bundle's base.
    marker: none

# Named lexical rules the fields reference. The module fragments
# (iso_*, iec_*, en_*, supplement_*, edition_*) are merged beside them.
grammar:
  digit: "%x30-39"
  alpha: '%x41-5A / %x61-7A'

fields:
  # The head token: the national body token, the designation faces
  # that ARE the designation ("PAS 003"), and the standalone-AMD head
  # (the face-only designation) — cen's publisher-type rule.
  publisher:
    pattern: '("BS" / "PAS" / "PD" / "DD" / "TS" / "AMD")'
    kind: string
  number:
    # The number carries a glued trailing letter ("BS 1000A:1961",
    # "PD 6481C:1977" — the coded column keeps it in the number). The
    # letter is UPPER-case only: the coded flavor rejects the lower-case
    # spelling ("PD 854a:1951", a negative-corpus row).
    pattern: '1*(%x30-39) [%x41-5A]'
    kind: string
  part:
    # The printed part: numeric ("107.2"), dotted ("107.2"), letter-led
    # ("A1", "B2"), multi-level ("1.3.3") — the coded part column keeps
    # the whole printed run.
    pattern: '1*(digit / alpha) *(("." / "-") 1*(digit / alpha))'
    kind: string
  year:
    pattern: '4digit'
    kind: string
  adopted:
    # The adopted run: an EN/CEN/CLC/HD/ENV/ES/CR/CWA/ISO/IEC/CISPR
    # lead token and the rest of the document face, ending before BSI's
    # own supplement run (the item rule the supplements declaration
    # compiles). CISPR is NOT a lead: the coded flavor routes "BS CISPR"
    # to its aerospace series (a family outside this surface), so the
    # composed flavor refuses it rather than mis-representing the class.
    # The IEC-internal runs ("/AMD1/FRAG1") cannot start a declared
    # item, so they stay inside the run the hook delegates.
    pattern: '( ( "EN" / "CEN" / "CLC" / "HD" / "ENV" / "ES" / "CR" / "CWA" / "ISO" / "IEC" ) ( *( !(bsi_supplement) ( %x01-09 / %x0B-10FFFF ) ) ) )'
    kind: string
    builder_only: true

# The scheme's calendar: the publication year of the document.
date:
  fields: [year]

templates:
  # The canonical face: the head alternation picks the first alternative
  # whose direct fields captured — the adoption face (the national head
  # over the adopted document), else the designation face. BSI's
  # plus-separated amendment run follows.
  canonical: '({publisher} " " {adopted} / {publisher} " " {number} ["-" {part}] [":" {year}]) [{supplements}]'

urn:
  # The coded urn:bsi:… form: the publisher downcased ("bs" — the coded
  # generator's fallback token; a designation face whose publisher is
  # its own token prints the fallback here too), the identity read
  # ROOT-THROUGH on the adoption wrappers (urn:bsi:bs:1073:-2:2002),
  # the part behind its dash, the year, the wrapper's own edition face
  # (v1), the designation's type abbr (skipping "BS" itself) and the
  # typed trio's stage segment (":stage.published" — the coded
  # generator's own comparison, which a String stage_code passes).
  namespace: bsi
  official:
    - { field: publisher, lower: true }
    - { field: number }
    - { field: part, affix: "-" }
    - { field: subpart, affix: "-" }
    - { date: [year] }
    - { field: edition, affix: "v" }
    - { type_abbr: { skip: BS } }
    - { stage_code: { published: true, marker: "stage." } }
  schema:
    # The coded schema's atom table, narrowed to the columns this
    # surface declares (the coded schema carries every family's atoms;
    # a compiled flavor declares what its model holds). The publisher
    # reads the component's body (the nested {"body": "DD"} shape the
    # serialization declaration keeps); the typed trio's components
    # serialize every registry field, so each field is its own atom.
    atoms:
      - { path: publisher.body, prefix: pubbody }
      - { path: part, prefix: part }
      - { path: year, prefix: year }
      - { path: edition, prefix: ed }
      - { path: type.abbr, prefix: typeabbr }
      - { path: type.name, prefix: typename }
      - { path: type.type_code, prefix: typetypecode }
      - { path: stage.abbr, prefix: stageabbr }
      - { path: stage.name, prefix: stagename }
      - { path: stage.stage_code, prefix: stagecode }
      - { path: stage.harmonized_stages, prefix: stagehs, kind: list }
      - { path: typed_stage.abbr, prefix: tsabbr, kind: list }
      - { path: typed_stage.name, prefix: tsname }
      - { path: typed_stage.code, prefix: tscode }
      - { path: typed_stage.stage_code, prefix: tsstagecode }
      - { path: typed_stage.type_code, prefix: tstypecode }
      - { path: typed_stage.harmonized_stages, prefix: tshs, kind: list }
      - { path: identifiers, prefix: ids, kind: ids }
    types:
      - { type: "pubid:bsi:adopted-european-norm", token: aen, core: [] }
      - { type: "pubid:bsi:adopted-international-standard", token: ais, core: [] }
      - { type: "pubid:bsi:amendment", token: amd, core: [number] }
      - { type: "pubid:bsi:british-standard", token: bs, core: [number] }
      - { type: "pubid:bsi:consolidated-identifier", token: consol, core: [] }
      - { type: "pubid:bsi:corrigendum", token: cor, core: [number] }
      - { type: "pubid:bsi:draft-document", token: dd, core: [number] }
      - { type: "pubid:bsi:published-document", token: pd, core: [number] }
      - { type: "pubid:bsi:publicly-available-specification", token: pas, core: [number] }
      - { type: "pubid:bsi:technical-specification", token: ts, core: [number] }

# The MR-slug hooks (the coded columns): the number-part fused, the year.
# The publisher segment is the shared model's (the captured head token).
mr:
  number: { join: [number, part], glue: "-" }
  year: { field: year }

# REQUIRED. The live test panel: real corpus shapes, one per family; each
# positive parses and renders as declared under the canonical face; each
# negative fails to parse (every negative verified against the coded
# flavor first — they are its rejections or its families outside this
# surface).
examples:
  positives:
    - input: "BS 10005:1995"
      renders: "BS 10005:1995"
    - input: "BS 1016-107.2:1991"
      renders: "BS 1016-107.2:1991"
    - input: "BS 1344-A1:1960"
      renders: "BS 1344-A1:1960"
    - input: "PD 5730"
      renders: "PD 5730"
    - input: "PAS 003:1994"
      renders: "PAS 003:1994"
    - input: "DD 136-2:1986"
      renders: "DD 136-2:1986"
    - input: "TS 1:1995"
      renders: "TS 1:1995"
    - input: "AMD 11015"
      renders: "AMD 11015"
    - input: "AMD 6262"
      renders: "AMD 6262"
    - input: "BS EN 1073-2:2002"
      renders: "BS EN 1073-2:2002"
    - input: "BS EN ISO 105-B06:2020"
      renders: "BS EN ISO 105-B06:2020"
    - input: "BS EN IEC 61851-1:2019"
      renders: "BS EN IEC 61851-1:2019"
    - input: "BS ISO 8601:2019"
      renders: "BS ISO 8601:2019"
    - input: "BS IEC 60747-8:2000"
      renders: "BS IEC 60747-8:2000"
    - input: "BS HD 60269-3"
      renders: "BS HD 60269-3"
    - input: "DD CEN ISO/TS 12180-1:2007"
      renders: "DD CEN ISO/TS 12180-1:2007"
    - input: "DD CLC/TS 50131-2-2:2004"
      renders: "DD CLC/TS 50131-2-2:2004"
    - input: "BS EN IEC 60601-1/FRAG1"
      renders: "BS EN IEC 60601-1/FRAG1"
    - input: "BS EN IEC 61535/AMD1/FRAG1"
      renders: "BS EN IEC 61535/AMD1/FRAG1"
    - input: "BS 10125:2014+A1:2016"
      renders: "BS 10125:2014+A1:2016"
    - input: "BS EN 1005-1:2001+A1:2008"
      renders: "BS EN 1005-1:2001+A1:2008"
    - input: "BS 646:1958+A2:2013"
      renders: "BS 646:1958+A2:2013"
  negatives:
    - "nonsense"
    - "BS"
    - "EN 1325"
    - "ISO 9001:2015"
    - "BS 2X 26:2001"
    - "DISC PD 0005:1995"
    - "BS A 103:2025"
    - "BSI Flex 1886 v2.0:2024-09"
    - "BS 7671 AMD2"
    - "BS 1000[9]:1971"
    - "BS 1580:Parts 1 and 2:1962"
    - "BS CISPR 12:1997"
    - "14/30300822 DC"
    - "NA to BS EN 1996-1-2:2005"
    - "BS 7722:2006 BOOK"
    - "BS 31100:2021 ExComm"
    - "BS 1425:Supplement No. 1:1966"
    - "BS 185 Index:1962"
    - "BS 2782-10:Method 1006:1978"
    - "BS 1902-2.3:Addendum No.  1:1976"
